# N-Eye — Gate lifecycle

Every major gate:

READ → VERIFY BASELINE → PLAN → IMPLEMENT → TARGETED TEST → INTEGRATE → ADVERSARIAL SELF-REVIEW → FIX SAFE IN-SCOPE DEFECTS → REGRESSION TESTS → RE-AUDIT → FULL REGRESSION → REAL-RUNTIME VERIFY WHERE APPLICABLE → MEASURE → EXPLAINABILITY COMMENTS → UPDATE CONTEXT.md → UPDATE UNDERSTANDING.md IF NEEDED → ADR/RECOMMENDATIONS → COMMIT ONLY WHEN ASKED AND VERIFIED → EVIDENCE REPORT.

Comments: code is WHAT; comments are WHY / TRUST / PRIVACY / RISK / LIFECYCLE (1–2 lines). Boundary modules state what may cross and what must never cross.

Do not implement T007/008 (OCR, ROI, visual grounding, adaptive perception) unless the human explicitly opens that gate.

After every major gate: update `docs/CONTEXT.md` to match source and this-run evidence.
